From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 08:33:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 108/121] spec: sparse target-only sampling verify on the
 top-KP logits

When every request in a sampling batch has top_k <= 248, the target-only
verify no longer builds full-vocabulary probabilities (softmax, radix
top-k renorm, AIR top-p renorm, min-p, zeros draft buffer, full-row final
draw). It takes torch.topk over the logits (KP = next_pow2(max top_k + 8)),
computes temperature/top-k/top-p/min-p on the KP values in one Triton
kernel (ties kept as FlashInfer does), and walks the tree on the sparse
rows with the final draw's cumulative sum in token-id order, so equal
coins give equal tokens up to rounding.

Off by default: SGLANG_OPT_SPEC_SPARSE_VERIFY=1. Greedy, RS and batches
with a request without top_k keep their current branches.

GPU check against the real dense kernels (flash-next-bench
bench/sv/test_sparse_verify.py): identical kept sets including bf16 ties,
max |dp| 4e-7, identical accept paths and tokens in 480/480 equal-coin
trees, chi2 p 0.13-0.82; verify GPU time 326-396 us -> 74-82 us
(bs 1-4, 4-16 draft tokens), of which torch.topk is 65-76 us.

